<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Workflow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <Workflow> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        NEW FILE, 2026-08-19. BOV_Submission__c had no workflow metadata before this change.

        🔴 [CORRECTED 2026-08-21: THIS SENTENCE NOW READS "FOUR FIELD UPDATES", NOT TWO. The
        "NO WORKFLOW RULE" half stands unchanged and applies to all four; so does the prohibition
        two paragraphs down.] TWO FIELD UPDATES, NO WORKFLOW RULE. Both are fired ONLY by
        approvalProcesses/BOV_Submission__c.Broker_Finalize_Approval - Approved as its
        finalApprovalActions, Rejected as its finalRejectionActions. Do not add a <rules>
        element: an active rule writing Approval_Status__c would advance the parent Disposition
        on an ordinary edit of a BOV submission.

        THE CHILD-OBJECT HALF OF D-1. Unlike the three Disposition-target approvals, this one
        does NOT need a Queueable: Broker_Finalize_Approval's recordEditability = AdminOnly locks
        the SUBMISSION, and the record the trigger has to write is the PARENT Disposition, which
        is not locked. BovSubmissionTriggerHandler therefore updates the parent SYNCHRONOUSLY
        with allOrNone = false in SYSTEM mode - the same shape ContractExecutionService already
        uses for its disposition arm.

        ⚠ THE TRIGGER REQUIRES BOTH CONDITIONS, NOT JUST THIS ONE. It advances the parent from
        BOV Outreach to Broker Selection only when Approval_Status__c reads Approved AND
        Submission_Status__c reads 'Selected'. Those are two distinct picklists on this object
        and they are not interchangeable: the first is the principals' sign-off, the second is
        the team's pick. It also requires the parent to be CURRENTLY on BOV Outreach - that
        idempotency guard is what makes a later broker replacement safe.

        ⚠ NAMING. agent-output/design-requirements.md A-5 transcribed these as
        Set_BOV_Approval_Approved / Set_BOV_Approval_Rejected and flagged the spelling as open
        (its section 6, open naming item 1). Set_Broker_* was chosen instead, to match the
        approval process that fires them (Broker_Finalize_Approval) and the business event
        ("the broker is approved"), and it is used consistently here and in that approval file.
        Nothing in Apex references a field update by name, so this is the only pair of files
        that has to agree.

        DEPLOY ORDER - LOAD-BEARING. This file must land BEFORE
        approvalProcesses/BOV_Submission__c.Broker_Finalize_Approval, which fails to deploy if a
        field update it names does not exist; and both field updates require
        objects/BOV_Submission__c/fields/Approval_Status__c.field-meta.xml.

        =====================================================================================
        2026-08-21 - TWO MORE FIELD UPDATES, ON A THIRD FIELD:
        Set_Broker_Approval_Pending AND Clear_Broker_Approval_Pending.
        =====================================================================================
        🔴 THEY WRITE Approval_Pending__c, WHICH IS A THIRD, DISTINCT FIELD FROM BOTH
        Approval_Status__c AND Submission_Status__c. The paragraph above already warns that the
        first two are not interchangeable; this makes three. In one line each:
            Submission_Status__c  the TEAM'S PICK
            Approval_Status__c    the PRINCIPALS' OUTCOME
            Approval_Pending__c   whether a decision is still OUTSTANDING (the new one)
        A Selected submission with a live approval reads Approval_Pending__c = true and
        Approval_Status__c BLANK. Do not treat a blank Approval_Status__c as "not submitted".

        WHAT FIRES THEM. Broker_Finalize_Approval, on all four transitions:
            initialSubmissionActions -> Set_Broker_Approval_Pending    (true)
            finalApprovalActions     -> Clear_Broker_Approval_Pending  (false, as a SECOND
                                        action alongside Set_Broker_Approval_Approved)
            finalRejectionActions    -> Clear_Broker_Approval_Pending  (false, as a SECOND
                                        action alongside Set_Broker_Approval_Rejected)
            recallActions            -> Clear_Broker_Approval_Pending  (false)

        WHY THE FLAG LIVES ON THIS OBJECT AND NOT DIRECTLY ON THE DISPOSITION. The button being
        hidden is on the DISPOSITION's page, and a FlexiPage visibility rule can only read a
        field on the record it is rendering. This approval targets the SUBMISSION, and
        BOV_Submission__c.Disposition__c is a LOOKUP, not Master Detail, so a cross object field
        update cannot reach the parent and a roll up summary cannot either. The value is stored
        here and BovSubmissionTriggerHandler mirrors it up in after update context, the same
        synchronous parent write shape this file's note above already describes for the
        approval half.

        ⚠ APPROVED AND REJECTED BOTH FIRE TWO ACTIONS NOW, AND THE PAIRINGS MATTER. Do not
        replace Set_Broker_Approval_Approved or Set_Broker_Approval_Rejected with the clear;
        the clear is an ADDITION alongside each. Removing either original would stop the parent
        Disposition advancing on approval.

        ⚠ BOTH HALVES ARRIVE IN ONE TRIGGER PASS on approval and on rejection, because the two
        field updates land in the same save. afterUpdate therefore sees Approval_Status__c and
        Approval_Pending__c change together.

        reevaluateOnChange stays false on both, for the reason already given above. Do not add a
        <rules> element for these either.

        DEPLOY ORDER for the new pair: objects/BOV_Submission__c/fields/Approval_Pending__c
        .field-meta.xml must land first, and this file before Broker_Finalize_Approval.
    -->
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>Clear_Broker_Approval_Pending</fullName>
        <description>Clears the broker approval pending flag. Fired by Broker_Finalize_Approval on all three terminal transitions: final approval, final rejection and recall. BovSubmissionTriggerHandler mirrors it onto the parent Disposition.</description>
        <field>Approval_Pending__c</field>
        <literalValue>0</literalValue>
        <name>Clear Broker Approval Pending</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>Set_Broker_Approval_Approved</fullName>
        <description>Final approval action of Broker_Finalize_Approval. Sets Approval Status to Approved, which BovSubmissionTriggerHandler reads to move the parent Disposition from BOV Outreach to Broker Selection and stamp Selected Broker.</description>
        <field>Approval_Status__c</field>
        <literalValue>Approved</literalValue>
        <name>Set Broker Approval Approved</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>Set_Broker_Approval_Pending</fullName>
        <description>Sets the broker approval pending flag. Fired as an initialSubmissionActions entry by Broker_Finalize_Approval. BovSubmissionTriggerHandler mirrors it onto the parent Disposition, where it hides the Submit Selected Broker action.</description>
        <field>Approval_Pending__c</field>
        <literalValue>1</literalValue>
        <name>Set Broker Approval Pending</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>Set_Broker_Approval_Rejected</fullName>
        <description>Final rejection action of Broker_Finalize_Approval. Sets Approval Status to Rejected. No stage moves: the Disposition stays at BOV Outreach so the team can pick a different broker and resubmit.</description>
        <field>Approval_Status__c</field>
        <literalValue>Rejected</literalValue>
        <name>Set Broker Approval Rejected</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
</Workflow>
